Hello,

I just updated for NetHack 3.4.3:

* itemcat (adds I - Unidentified Items, P - Items just
taken out [or P - Items just Picked up, resp.] and perhaps r - Items
known to be Rustprone [depending on options/compile time settings, see
the diff for more info]) and

* qt_posix (use alternative of non-POSIX scandir() in qt code, so you
can compile nicely on non-BSDish systems). Perhaps the DevTeam should
consider replacing this call with something else in a future release?

